bool XCFImageFormat::loadTileRLE(QDataStream &xcf_io, uchar *tile, int image_size,
                                 int data_length, qint32 bpp)
{
    // ...
    for (int i = 0; i < bpp; ++i) {
        data = tile + i;
        int count = 0;
        int size = image_size;
        while (size > 0) {
            // ...
            while (length-- > 0) {
                *data = *xcfdata++;
                data += sizeof(QRgb);
            }
        }
    }
}
```

The `bpp` parameter comes from `loadHierarchy`, which reads it from the file and then corrects it based on `layer.type`. But what if the correction doesn't happen? Let me look at `loadHierarchy` again:

```cpp
